      "evidence": "In template/scripts/shared_workspace.py, `audit()` returns `(None, [Finding(... 'POSIX group-mode enforcement unavailable; no changes made')])` when `posix_available()` is false. The old `preflight()` did `if group is None: return`. The new `preflight_with_report` does `if group is None: raise SharedWorkspaceError(findings[0].message)`. The registry condition guards this with `shared_workspace_applicable`, but the finish_task.py main loop (`for shared_root in (integration, work)...: repaired = preflight_with_report(shared_root)`) does not. A finish run on a non-POSIX platform therefore regresses from a silent skip to a hard failure.",
      "id": "finish-permission-step-refuses-on-non-posix",
      "severity": "advisory",
      "summary": "finish_task.py now calls shared_workspace.preflight_with_report unconditionally. Where POSIX group enforcement is unavailable, it raises instead of returning silently, as the old preflight did."
